## 2. Server — Layered Architecture

The server follows a clean **layered / dependency-injection** pattern wired together in [container.ts](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/server/src/container.ts).

```mermaid
graph TD
    R["Routes\n(Express Router)"]
    MW["Middlewares\n(Auth · Rate-Limit · Logger · Error)"]
    C["Controllers\n(HTTP Adapters)"]
    S["Services\n(Business Logic)"]
    REPO["Repositories\n(Data Access Layer)"]
    M["Mongoose Models\n(Schema / ODM)"]
    DB[("MongoDB")]

    R --> MW --> C --> S --> REPO --> M --> DB
```

### Key Layers

| Layer | Files | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| **Routes** | `routes/*.ts` | Mount endpoints, attach middlewares |
| **Middlewares** | `middlewares/` | Auth (JWT), error handler, rate limiter, logger |
| **Controllers** | `controllers/` | Validate request, call service, send response |
| **Services** | `services/` | Business rules, orchestrate repositories |
| **Repositories** | `repositories/` | Abstract Mongoose CRUD operations |
| **Models** | `models/` | Mongoose schemas & document types |

