## 4. Real-Time Socket.IO Layer

```mermaid
graph LR
    subgraph Client
        CE["Code Editor"]
        Chat["Chat / Messaging"]
        RM["Room Management"]
    end

    subgraph SocketManager["Socket.IO Server"]
        SM["SocketManager.ts\n(initializes namespaces)"]
        EH["EventHandler.ts"]
        EE["EditorEvents.ts\n(CRDT-like sync)"]
        IE["InvitationEvents.ts"]
        ME["MessageEvents.ts"]
        RE["RequestEvents.ts"]
        UE["UserEvents.ts\n(online presence)"]
    end

    subgraph Redis["Redis Adapter"]
        PUB["Pub/Sub\n(multi-instance scaling)"]
    end

    CE <-->|code-change, cursor| EE
    Chat <-->|send-message| ME
    RM <-->|invite, kick, join| IE & RE

    SM --> EH --> EE & IE & ME & RE & UE
    SM <--> PUB
```

> **Scaling**: The Socket.IO server uses `@socket.io/redis-adapter` so multiple app replicas (2 in production via Docker) share real-time state through Redis pub/sub.

---

## 5. Code Execution Pipeline

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as Client (Editor)
    participant API as /api/execute
    participant P as Piston Engine
    U->>API: POST { language, code }
    API->>P: POST /api/v2/execute
    P-->>API: { stdout, stderr, exitCode }
    API-->>U: Execution result
```

- **Local / Docker**: Uses the official `ghcr.io/engineer-man/piston` container (supports 50+ languages, requires `privileged: true`).
- **Cloud (Render)**: Uses the custom **Piston-Lite** ([piston/server.js](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/piston/server.js)) — a lightweight Express server that runs Python & JavaScript via `child_process.exec` with a 5-second timeout.

---

## 6. Background Jobs (BullMQ)

```mermaid
graph LR
    SC["Scheduler\n(node-cron)"] -->|enqueue job| Q["BullMQ Queue\n(Redis-backed)"]
    Q --> W["Worker\n(subscriptionWorker.ts)"]
    W --> DB[(MongoDB)]
    W --> MAIL[Nodemailer\nExpiry emails]
```

- **Queue**: `bullmq/queues/` — defines `subscriptionQueue`
- **Scheduler**: `bullmq/schedulers/subscriptionScheduler.ts` — fires subscription expiry checks on a cron schedule
- **Worker**: `bullmq/workers/subscriptionWorker.ts` — processes jobs, expires subscriptions, sends emails

> In production, scheduler & worker run as **separate Docker containers** to avoid blocking the main API process.

---

## 7. GraphQL Layer

| File | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [graphql/index.ts](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/server/src/graphql/index.ts) | Mounts Apollo Server as Express middleware |
| `graphql/schema/` | GraphQL type definitions |
| `graphql/resolvers/` | Resolver functions (call services) |

The client uses **Apollo Client** to query/mutate via `/graphql`.

---

## 8. Subscription & Payment Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant API as Server REST
    participant RZP as Razorpay
    participant DB as MongoDB

    U->>API: POST /api/payment/create-order
    API->>RZP: Create Razorpay order
    RZP-->>API: orderId + key
    API-->>U: Payment details
    U->>RZP: Complete payment (client SDK)
    RZP-->>U: payment_id, signature
    U->>API: POST /api/payment/verify
    API->>API: Verify HMAC signature
    API->>DB: Create Payment + UserSubscription records
    API-->>U: Subscription activated
```

---

## 9. Deployment Topology

### Docker Compose (Self-hosted / Local Prod)

```mermaid
graph TD
    subgraph Docker Network ["Docker bridge network: backend"]
        FE["frontend\nNext.js :3000"]
        NGINX["nginx\n:5000 (load balancer)"]
        APP1["app replica 1\n:5000"]
        APP2["app replica 2\n:5000"]
        WORKER["worker\n(BullMQ consumer)"]
        SCHED["scheduler\n(BullMQ producer)"]
        REDIS_D["redis:alpine"]
        PISTON_D["piston\n:2000"]
        LOKI_D["grafana/loki\n:3100"]
        PROMTAIL_D["grafana/promtail"]
        GRAFANA_D["grafana\n:3001"]
    end

    Internet -->|port 3000| FE
    Internet -->|port 5000| NGINX
    Internet -->|port 3001| GRAFANA_D
    NGINX --> APP1 & APP2
    APP1 <--> REDIS_D
    APP2 <--> REDIS_D
    APP1 --> PISTON_D
    WORKER --> REDIS_D
    SCHED --> REDIS_D
    PROMTAIL_D --> LOKI_D --> GRAFANA_D
```

### Kubernetes (k8s/)

| Manifest | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [backend-deployment.yaml](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/k8s/backend-deployment.yaml) | Express server Deployment |
| [backend-service.yaml](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/k8s/backend-service.yaml) | ClusterIP Service for backend |
| [frontend-deployment.yaml](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/k8s/frontend-deployment.yaml) | Next.js Deployment |
| [frontend-service.yaml](file:///d:/projects/Next%20Project/CODIE/k8s/frontend-service.yaml) | LoadBalancer / NodePort for frontend |

